	'run_p' => 'A dedicated grass lawn enclosed by a 1.4 m fence with secure double gates. Lit after dusk, with fresh running water, shade sails and clean bowls. Kofi walks the final 21:30 evening round before the gates close at 22:00.',
	's_about_1_b' => 'Ashiato Hotel stands at 7 Linden Row in Alder Bay, occupying a seaside guesthouse originally built in 1931. The building opened in its current form in 2016, founded by Ines Moreau as a dedicated retreat for people travelling with dogs. Rather than treating dogs as an awkward exception or charging hidden penalties, we planned fourteen rooms around canine comfort, safety, and routine. Dogs here are treated as genuine guests from the minute they arrive at our doors. Our grounds include an enclosed 1,200 square metre meadow dog run, and our rooms welcome up to two dogs weighing up to 40 kg each. The atmosphere remains calm, quiet, and rooted in the coastal landscape.',
	's_about_1_h' => 'From a 1931 Guesthouse to Ashiato',
	's_about_2_b' => 'Seven people run Ashiato Hotel every day with defined responsibilities. Ines Moreau founded the hotel, oversees the front desk, and kneels to greet every arriving dog by name. Mei Chen manages all bookings, answering every enquiry within 24 hours. Kofi Mensah oversees the evening desk and the dog run, walking the final 21:30 inspection round. Hana Lindqvist serves as our dedicated dog host and sitter for guests who step out. Amara Okoye runs our grooming room, handling gentle wash and dry sessions and nail trims. Rafael Ortiz bakes our welcome biscuits fresh in the terrace kitchen. Housekeeper Theo Brandt ensures every dog bed is stripped, washed, and sanitised between visits.',
	's_about_2_h' => 'The Team Behind Ashiato',
	's_about_3_b' => 'Life at the hotel follows a steady rhythm tuned to canine habits and quiet seaside hours. The dog run opens at 06:00 every morning so early risers can stretch on the grass. Breakfast is served from 07:30 to 10:00 on the terrace, where dogs relax beside outdoor tables. Guest check-in runs from 15:00 to 20:00, while check-out is at 11:00. In the evening, the terrace reopens from 18:00 to 21:00 for drinks and light snacks. Kofi Mensah conducts his final safety inspection of the dog run at 21:30 before the gates close at 22:00. The front desk operates daily from 07:00 to 23:00, with a night bell available afterwards.',
	's_about_3_h' => 'The Daily Rhythm',
	's_book_1_b' => 'At Ashiato, reservations follow one clear three-step path: Ask, Confirm, and Arrive. First, submit our booking form or write directly to stay@ashiatohotel.example detailing your requested arrival and departure dates, room choice, and your dog\'s name, breed, and weight. Second, Mei Chen confirms your stay by replying personally within 24 hours with a secure link to pay the 20% deposit. Third, you arrive between 15:00 and 20:00 on your arrival date. The front desk greets your dog by name, introduces you to the paw-wash station, and escorts you to your room where fresh bowls and bedding await.',
	's_book_1_h' => 'Our Three-Step Booking Process',
	's_book_2_b' => 'All room rates include daily terrace breakfast for human guests. Balcony Rooms are €148 per night for two guests. Garden Rooms with private fenced patio lawns are €168 per night for two guests. Two-Dog Rooms with twin raised dog beds are €196 per night for two guests and two dogs. The Linden Suite is €245 per night for up to four guests. The dog stay fee is €18 per dog per night, covering bedding, bowls, towels, welcome kit, and dog run access. Optional dog sitting with Hana is €16 per hour, and wash and dry grooming with Amara is €35 per dog.',
	's_book_2_h' => 'Room Rates and Additional Services',
	's_book_3_b' => 'To confirm your reservation, a 20% deposit is payable upon booking following Mei Chen\'s email. We offer free cancellation on all bookings up to 7 days before your scheduled arrival date. We welcome up to two dogs per room, with each dog weighing up to 40 kg. Check-in takes place between 15:00 and 20:00, while check-out is at 11:00 on the day of departure. Please ensure your dog\'s rabies and DHPP vaccination records and 30-day flea and tick treatment certificates are ready to present at reception upon your arrival at Linden Row.',
	's_book_3_h' => 'Booking Terms and Cancellation Policy',
	's_cafe_1_b' => 'Breakfast is served daily between 07:30 and 10:00 on our outdoor terrace, and is included in the nightly room rate for all human guests. Dogs on leads are warmly welcomed at every terrace table. We provide fresh water bowls at each outdoor seating spot so dogs stay refreshed while you enjoy fresh bread, coffee, and morning tea. To ensure comfort for all hotel visitors, our indoor dining room is kept dog-free, giving guests who prefer an indoor setting a dedicated quiet space. On sunny or misty mornings alike, the terrace offers a peaceful start to the day by the sea.',
	's_cafe_1_h' => 'Breakfast on the Terrace',
	's_cafe_2_b' => 'Rafael Ortiz leads the terrace kitchen, preparing food for guests and special treats for our four-legged visitors. Every dog staying at Ashiato receives one of Rafael\'s house-baked welcome biscuits upon arrival. He bakes these biscuits using simple, wholesome ingredients suitable for canine digestion, free from added salt, seasonings, or preservatives. During the day, Rafael also prepares healthy dog-friendly snacks that can be ordered directly to terrace tables, alongside fresh water bowls and shaded resting mats. It ensures your dog feels as pampered during breakfast as you do.',
	's_cafe_2_h' => 'Rafael\'s Terrace Kitchen and Dog Treats',
	's_cafe_3_b' => 'As daylight softens over Alder Bay, the terrace reopens from 18:00 to 21:00 for evening drinks and conversation. Guests can unwind after a long walk along the coast while their dogs rest quietly under the tables on their leads. Warm blankets and evening sea breezes create an unhurried, comfortable atmosphere. It is an ideal spot to compare walking routes or simply relax before Kofi Mensah conducts his 21:30 evening inspection round of the dog run. When the terrace closes at 21:00, the night remains peaceful and still.',
	's_cafe_3_h' => 'Evenings on the Terrace',
	's_contact_1_b' => 'The front desk at Ashiato is staffed daily from 07:00 to 23:00. You can reach our reception team by telephone at +00 44 3100 2468 or by emailing stay@ashiatohotel.example. Outside of daytime hours, an emergency night bell is located beside the main entrance for arriving or resident guests. Founder Ines Moreau and bookings manager Mei Chen personally oversee incoming correspondence, answering room enquiries and travel questions within 24 hours. Whether you need advice regarding dog weight limits, room suitability, or local walking routes, our team is always ready to assist.',
	's_contact_1_h' => 'Direct Contact and Reception Hours',
	's_contact_2_b' => 'Ashiato Hotel is located at 7 Linden Row in Alder Bay. For guests arriving by train, Alder Bay railway station is an easy 10-minute walk through town to our front door. If you are travelling by car, the hotel provides six dedicated on-site parking spaces in our private rear forecourt. A veterinary clinic is conveniently located just 6 minutes away by car, and the front desk keeps emergency contact details posted at reception. Please contact us in advance if you require assistance with luggage or parking on arrival.',
	's_contact_2_h' => 'Finding Us in Alder Bay',
	's_dog_run_1_b' => 'Located directly behind the hotel building, our dog run spans 1,200 square metres of natural grass. The entire perimeter is secured with a 1.4-metre high fence and accessed through a double-gate entry system to prevent accidental escapes. A dedicated small-dog corner offers a calmer space for smaller breeds who prefer quiet play. The field features a shade sail for sunny afternoons, a fresh water tap with drinking bowls, and benches where owners can relax. Waste bag dispensers and covered bins are placed at the entrance. It provides the ideal setting for off-lead exercise overlooking the Alder Bay coastline.',
	's_dog_run_1_h' => 'A Secure 1,200 m² Meadow',
	's_dog_run_2_b' => 'The dog run is open daily from 06:00 to 22:00, accommodating both early morning exercise and evening walks before bed. Low-glare lighting illuminates the main paths and central lawn after dusk so dogs can play safely after sunset. At 21:30 each evening, Kofi Mensah from our desk team walks his final inspection round of the grounds, checking fences, tidying equipment, and greeting guests enjoying the late air. The gates close promptly at 22:00 to preserve quiet for hotel guests sleeping in nearby ground-floor rooms. The main hotel front desk remains staffed until 23:00.',
	's_dog_run_2_h' => 'Hours, Lighting, and Evening Rounds',
	's_dog_run_3_b' => 'To keep the dog run enjoyable for everyone, owners must supervise their dogs at all times. Dogs must remain on their leads until both gates of the double-entry portal are securely closed. For health and safety reasons, female dogs in heat are not permitted in the dog run at any time. We ask all owners to clean up promptly after their dogs using the waste bags and bins provided. Dogs displaying signs of illness or aggression should be exercised on walking trails rather than in communal play areas. Fresh water should be refreshed regularly at the outdoor tap.',
	's_dog_run_3_h' => 'Dog Run Etiquette and Safety',
	's_dogs_1_b' => 'To keep our environment safe and comfortable, Ashiato welcomes dogs only; we do not accept cats or other pets. We accommodate up to two dogs per room, with a maximum weight limit of 40 kg per dog. At check-in, owners must present an up-to-date veterinary record confirming valid rabies and DHPP vaccinations. Additionally, all dogs must have received preventative flea and tick treatment within the last 30 days before arrival. Dogs may remain alone in your guest room for up to 2 hours, provided the Dog in room door card is displayed. For longer absences, our dedicated dog sitter Hana Lindqvist is available at €16 per hour.',
	's_dogs_1_h' => 'Our House Rules for Dogs',
	's_dogs_2_b' => 'Dogs must remain on a lead when moving through hallways, reception, and indoor shared corridors. On the outdoor terrace, dogs are warmly welcomed to join you for breakfast between 07:30 and 10:00, provided they remain on a lead beside your table where fresh water bowls are placed. The indoor dining room remains dog-free to accommodate all guest preferences. When returning from the beach or nearby trails, please use the paw-wash station at the main entrance, where warm water and clean towels make rinsing sand and mud simple. Off-lead play is reserved exclusively for our fully enclosed 1,200 square metre dog run, open daily from 06:00 to 22:00.',
	's_dogs_2_h' => 'Moving Through the Property',
	's_dogs_3_b' => 'Packing for your stay is straightforward because we supply the essentials. Please remember to bring your dog\'s vaccination certificate, a sturdy lead, and their regular food to prevent dietary upsets. You do not need to pack dog bedding, feeding dishes, or grooming towels. Every guest room is pre-stocked with a comfortable dog bed and blanket, two heavy ceramic bowls, fresh towels changed every day, and waste disposal bags. Upon arrival, Ines Moreau and the desk team greet your dog with a house-baked welcome biscuit, ensuring they settle into their coastal stay right away.',
	's_dogs_3_h' => 'What to Pack for Your Dog',
	's_faq_10_b' => 'Booking follows one simple, three-part process: Ask, Confirm, and Arrive. First, you ask by submitting the request form on our website or sending an email to stay@ashiatohotel.example with your travel dates, room preference, and your dog\'s name, breed, and weight. Next, Mei Chen confirms by replying within 24 hours with a link to pay the 20% deposit. Finally, you arrive between 15:00 and 20:00, where Ines Moreau and the desk team meet your dog by name.',
	's_faq_10_h' => 'How do I book?',
	's_faq_1_b' => 'We welcome dogs weighing up to 40 kg per dog. When we founded Ashiato, we decided against arbitrary toy-breed-only restrictions, ensuring that large, well-mannered dogs like retrievers and Bernese mountain dogs are just as welcome as smaller terriers. The Varga family stayed in our Linden Suite with Bruno, a 39 kg Bernese, proving that larger dogs thrive here. We weigh each dog during check-in to confirm they meet our weight policy, and our rooms are generously proportioned to accommodate dogs of all eligible sizes comfortably.',
	's_faq_1_h' => 'How big can my dog be?',
	's_faq_2_b' => 'Yes, you may bring up to two dogs per room, provided each dog weighs 40 kg or less. We have three dedicated Two-Dog Rooms specifically designed for families travelling with a pair of dogs, featuring expanded floor layouts and two separate raised dog beds. Guests like Leah, who visits every spring with her two dachshunds Olive and Fig, find this layout ideal. Two dogs can also be accommodated in our Garden Rooms, Balcony Rooms, and the Linden Suite. The standard dog stay fee of €18 applies per dog per night.',
	's_faq_2_h' => 'Can I bring two dogs?',
	's_faq_3_b' => 'Dogs may stay alone in your room for up to 2 hours, provided they are settled and you display the Dog in room door card outside your door. This allows you to step out for a short errand or dinner with peace of mind. If you expect to be away for more than 2 hours, or if your dog is prone to anxiety when left alone, you must book our dog sitter Hana Lindqvist. Hana is available between 08:00 and 21:00 at €16 per hour to keep your dog company.',
	's_faq_3_h' => 'Can my dog stay alone in the room?',
	's_faq_4_b' => 'Yes, our 1,200 square metre dog run is completely enclosed by a secure 1.4-metre high fence. Entry and exit are controlled via a double-gate security portal to prevent any possibility of dogs slipping out when guests enter. The run is open daily from 06:00 to 22:00 and is illuminated with gentle lighting after dusk so dogs can play safely into the evening. It also features a shade sail, fresh water tap, and small-dog corner. Kofi Mensah carries out his final inspection round at 21:30 each evening.',
	's_faq_4_h' => 'Is the dog run fenced?',
	's_faq_5_b' => 'You only need to bring three things: your dog\'s official vaccination record, a reliable lead, and their usual food. The vaccination record must show current rabies and DHPP immunisations, along with flea and tick treatment administered within the past 30 days. You do not need to bring bulky gear. Ashiato provides a freshly laundered dog bed, blanket, two heavy ceramic bowls, clean dog towels changed daily, and waste bags. Ines Moreau and the desk team will also greet your dog with a fresh welcome biscuit baked by Rafael Ortiz.',
	's_faq_5_h' => 'What do I need to bring?',
	's_faq_6_b' => 'Yes, dogs are warmly welcomed on our outdoor terrace during breakfast from 07:30 to 10:00. Your dog must remain on a lead beside your table, where we place individual water bowls. Breakfast for human guests is included with every room booking. However, dogs are not permitted inside the enclosed indoor dining room, which remains reserved for guests who prefer to dine without animals nearby. If the weather is windy or brisk, the terrace features sheltered corners and warm blankets so you and your dog can enjoy breakfast together in comfort.',
	's_faq_6_h' => 'Can my dog come to breakfast?',
	's_faq_7_b' => 'Yes, the dog stay fee is €18 per dog per night. This fee is never a vague cleaning penalty; it directly covers dedicated amenities including your dog\'s bed and blanket laundered by Theo Brandt, two ceramic bowls, daily clean towels, waste bags, a welcome biscuit from Rafael Ortiz, and unlimited access to our 1,200 square metre dog run. Additional optional services include dog sitting with Hana Lindqvist at €16 per hour and grooming wash and dry sessions with Amara Okoye at €35 per dog.',
	's_faq_7_h' => 'Is there a dog fee?',
	's_faq_8_b' => 'If your dog is sensitive to corridor movement or unfamiliar night sounds, we recommend booking one of our Garden Rooms situated at the far end of the ground-floor corridor. These rooms are our quietest, with private fenced patios and minimal passing foot traffic. When Sam stayed with Juno, a rescue greyhound on her first holiday, this quiet setting helped Juno settle without disturbance. Please mention your dog\'s sensitivities when submitting your booking request so Mei Chen can allocate the most suitable room for your stay.',
	's_faq_8_h' => 'What if my dog barks at night?',
	's_faq_9_b' => 'Yes, there is an established veterinary practice located just 6 minutes away by car from the hotel. While we hope you never need it during a relaxing seaside holiday, our front desk keeps the practice\'s emergency contact details and direct telephone numbers immediately on hand at all hours. Our desk team is staffed daily from 07:00 to 23:00, with a night bell available after 23:00, so someone is always available to help you arrange directions or assistance if your dog becomes unwell.',
	's_faq_9_h' => 'Is there a vet nearby?',
	's_newsletter_1_b' => 'Four times each year, we send The Register Letter directly from our front desk to your email inbox. Each edition reflects the natural rhythm of Alder Bay across the seasons. In spring, we share updates on coastal walking routes, meadow blooms, and trail conditions following winter rains. In summer, we highlight quiet booking weeks and tips for beach walks with dogs. In autumn, we write about crisp evenings in our 1,200 square metre dog run under the dusk lighting. In winter, we announce upcoming seasonal rates and peaceful coastal retreat weekends.',
	's_newsletter_1_h' => 'Four Seasonal Dispatches Each Year',
	's_newsletter_2_b' => 'We believe email should be calm, useful, and respectful of your time. The Register Letter contains no third-party advertisements, aggressive countdown timers, or sponsored partnerships. It is written personally by Mei Chen and Ines Moreau to keep our community of dog lovers connected to our small hotel. You can request the letter using the form on this page or by writing to stay@ashiatohotel.example. If your travel plans change or you no longer wish to receive our seasonal news, you can unsubscribe at any moment with a single click.',
	's_newsletter_2_h' => 'A Thoughtful and Quiet Correspondence',
	's_rooms_1_b' => 'Ashiato features fourteen guest rooms divided across four distinct types. Our four Garden Rooms sit on the ground floor, each opening directly onto its own private fenced patio lawn where dogs can rest outdoors. Our six Balcony Rooms occupy the first floor, offering sea views and private balconies secured with protective mesh guards. For guests travelling with two canine companions, our three Two-Dog Rooms provide expanded floor plans equipped with two raised dog beds. Finally, our single Linden Suite provides spacious family accommodation, comfortably welcoming up to four guests alongside one or two dogs. Every room has easy-to-clean flooring and generous floor area.',
	's_rooms_1_h' => 'Four Layouts for Dogs and Their Owners',
	's_rooms_2_b' => 'Every booking at Ashiato includes eight fixed amenities to ensure effortless travel. In your room, you will find a dedicated dog bed and blanket, two heavy ceramic bowls, and clean dog towels changed daily by Theo Brandt. Waste bags are stocked at every door throughout the property. Guests enjoy unlimited access to our 1,200 square metre fenced dog run from 06:00 to 22:00, as well as our entrance paw-wash station equipped with warm water and fresh towels. Upon arrival, your dog receives a house-baked welcome biscuit prepared by Rafael Ortiz, along with a printed map detailing three scenic walking routes starting right from Linden Row.',
	's_rooms_2_h' => 'What Every Room Includes',
	's_rooms_3_b' => 'Nightly rates include breakfast for all human guests. Balcony Rooms are €148 per night for up to two guests and one to two dogs. Garden Rooms are €168 per night for up to two guests and one to two dogs. Two-Dog Rooms are €196 per night for two guests and two dogs. The Linden Suite is €245 per night for up to four guests and one to two dogs. Dog stays are €18 per dog per night, covering the bed, bowls, towels, welcome kit, and dog run access. A 20% deposit is required to confirm. Free cancellation is available up to 7 days before arrival. Up to 2 dogs per room, up to 40 kg each.',
	's_rooms_3_h' => 'Nightly Room Rates',
	's_the_stay_1_b' => 'Each stay at Ashiato automatically includes eight core services and amenities. In your room, we provide a dedicated dog bed and blanket, two heavy ceramic food and water bowls, and clean dog towels changed daily by housekeeping. We keep waste bags stocked at every door and station on the property. Guests have complete access to our enclosed 1,200 square metre dog run between 06:00 and 22:00. At the front entrance, a dedicated paw-wash station with warm water lets you rinse muddy paws after coastal outings. Upon arrival, your dog enjoys a house-baked welcome biscuit from Rafael Ortiz, along with a printed pocket map of three local walking trails.',
	's_the_stay_1_h' => 'Eight Inclusions with Every Booking',
	's_the_stay_2_b' => 'Our dedicated staff provide personalized support throughout your time with us. Hana Lindqvist, our resident dog host and sitter, is on hand between 08:00 and 21:00 to sit with your dog in your room or walk them for €16 per hour. In our dedicated grooming room, Amara Okoye provides complete 40-minute wash and dry treatments for €35 per dog, as well as gentle nail trims after beach walks. Behind the scenes, housekeeper Theo Brandt carefully strips, launders, and sanitises every dog bed and blanket between guest departures, ensuring pristine hygiene for every new arrival.',
	's_the_stay_2_h' => 'Personal Care by Hana, Amara, and Theo',
	's_the_stay_3_b' => 'We publish clear, fixed rates for every room and service. Balcony Rooms are €148 per night for two guests. Garden Rooms are €168 per night for two guests. Two-Dog Rooms are €196 per night for two guests and two dogs. The Linden Suite is €245 per night for up to four guests. The dog stay fee is €18 per dog per night, covering beds, bowls, daily towels, welcome kit, and run access. Dog sitting with Hana is €16 per hour from 08:00 to 21:00. Wash and dry with Amara is €35 per dog for 40 minutes. A 20% deposit is required to confirm. Free cancellation up to 7 days before arrival. Up to 2 dogs per room, up to 40 kg each.',
	's_the_stay_3_h' => 'Rates and Transparent Pricing',
	's_walks_1_b' => 'You do not need to drive to find wonderful walking trails during your stay at Ashiato. Three scenic walking routes begin right at our front door at 7 Linden Row. Each path has been carefully surveyed by our team for safety, trail quality, and canine interest. In your room welcome kit, you will find a printed pocket map detailing route turnings, surface conditions, water access points, and seasonal lead rules. When you return from your outing, our entrance paw-wash station and fresh towels are ready to clean sandy paws before you head upstairs to relax.',
	's_walks_1_h' => 'Three Routes Starting from Linden Row',
	's_walks_2_b' => 'The Linden Loop is a gentle 2.4-kilometre circuit taking approximately 35 minutes, following quiet residential roads and shoreline pavements around Alder Bay. It is flat, paved, and ideal for morning stretches before breakfast. For a longer coastal excursion, the Bay Dunes route covers 4.1 kilometres and takes around 70 minutes. This path winds over sand tracks, wooden boardwalks, and rolling dunes with open sea vistas. To protect nesting shorebirds, dogs must be kept on leads on the dunes from May to August. Please carry drinking water for your dog during warmer summer afternoons on this trail.',
	's_walks_2_h' => 'Linden Loop and Bay Dunes',
	's_walks_3_b' => 'The Alder Woods trail is our longest route, measuring 6 kilometres and requiring roughly 2 hours of easy walking. The path departs the hotel towards the coastal meadows before entering tall pine and alder woods. It offers shaded earthen trails, soft needles underfoot, and cool shelter on warm days. Dogs enjoy the rich woodland scents and gentle slopes. Because this is a natural woodland environment, we advise carrying fresh water and checking your dog for burs or twigs upon your return. Back at Ashiato, our groomer Amara Okoye can assist with coat brushing and paw care if needed.',
	's_walks_3_h' => 'Alder Woods Trail',
