	'welcome_h' => 'A front desk that kneels.',
	'welcome_p1' => 'Ashiato Hotel opened in 2016 inside a 1931 seaside guesthouse at 7 Linden Row in Alder Bay. The building was carefully renovated from the ground up to welcome dogs and their owners together, preserving the structure’s original coastal light while establishing fourteen dedicated rooms where dogs are never treated as an afterthought.',
	'welcome_p2' => 'Before you arrive, Ines Moreau and the desk team learn your dog’s name, breed and weight. When you walk through the entrance, the receptionist kneels down on the lobby floor to greet your dog at eye level, offering fresh water and a house-baked welcome biscuit while you sign the paper register.',
	'welcome_p3' => 'This is a small hotel designed entirely around how dogs live and travel. With an enclosed dog run, daily terrace breakfasts where dogs rest beside you, and quiet rooms with dedicated dog beds, your dog is treated as a guest in their own right throughout the stay.',
);
